# Design Narrative
# Mechanic: Unpredictable Cyclone replaces a cycling draw with the first library card sharing the cycled card's type and permits a free cast.
# Forcing: One Island pays for exactly one cycle. The sorcery skips a creature and reaches lethal Lava Axe; the creature finds only a summoning-sick Bear.
# AI behavior: The opponent has no decisions. Both cycling abilities are available, but only one can be paid for.
# Failure modes:
#   WIN = Boon of the Wish-Giver was cycled and Lava Axe dealt exact lethal damage.
#   LOSE = Curator of Mysteries was cycled, leaving no mana or attacker for a win this turn.
#   TIMEOUT = the replacement effect or free-cast decision did not complete.
# Card roles:
#   Unpredictable Cyclone — converts the chosen card type into a library search and free cast.
#   Boon of the Wish-Giver — the correct sorcery to cycle.
#   Curator of Mysteries — the tempting creature to cycle.
#   Grizzly Bears — the creature hit by the wrong choice and skipped by the right one.
#   Lava Axe — the exact-lethal sorcery reached by the right choice.
# Protocol path: Activate cycling, replace draw, cast the exiled matching card, and resolve it.
[metadata]
